  "source": {
    "path": "build/keyboard-controller-analog/rollback-time-bridge-postreset/vpi.c",
    "sha256": "54419fef0ac32cba3dc8e13790baabcede9e2bc9c26f55424d7ff8686f08215e",
    "getTimeExcerpt": "static double get_time(struct ng_vvp *ctx)\n{\n    static struct t_vpi_time now = { .type = vpiSimTime };\n    uint64_t                 ticks;\n\n    vpi_get_time(NULL, &now);\n    ticks = ((uint64_t)now.high << 32) + now.low;\n    return (double)ticks * ctx->tick_length;\n}"
  },
  "findings": [
    "The first changed bus sample timestamp is corroborated by bus_high/bus_low callback times from vpi_get_time, rather than only the formatted BUS_EDGE_PS text.",
    "At the largest voltage residual, the middle-step data_sink event is one HDL tick later than both other refinements; the coarse and finest node values nearly coincide while the middle value differs by about 3.16 mV. This is a localization clue, not proof of causation.",
    "File-adjacent BUS and TIME_AUDIT records are not a common timeline because stdout and stderr buffering differ. Use explicit event times and target-window records."
  ],
  "nextExperiment": "Use a bounded deterministic input-edge fixture around integer HDL tick boundaries to distinguish threshold localization, input application ordering and delta-to-tick conversion. Validate any candidate with unchanged controls before another full board refinement."
}
